Wire up the reload

     Context

     The reload is scaffolding only. The Action/Reload compound has five leaf states                                                                             
     (IntroInsertBullet, TurnCylinder, InsertNextBullet, CloseCylinder, Interrupt) that are                                                                                                         
     empty stubs with no exports, no transitions and no Travel calls, and nothing in the chart ever
     enters Reload. reloadTrigger is set in two places and consumed nowhere; reloadInterrupted is
     declared and never touched.

     The AnimationTree side is mostly built: SM_Reload is a nested machine at
     parameters/Reload/playback with InsertFirst / Turn / InsertNext / ToClose /
     RevolverReloadInterrupt / Close, reached through the root leaves
     RevolverRigReloadStartOpenCylinder{Hip,Aim}.

     Outcome: R reloads one round at a time until the cylinder is full or the reserve is dry, and a fire
     press during the insert loop aborts into the interrupt-to-close path.

     Decisions taken (confirmed with the user)

     1. Loop ends at a full cylinder or an empty reserve, whichever comes first. Each inserted round
        decrements reserveAmmo via the existing SubtractBulletFromTotalAmmo().
     2. A fire press mid-reload aborts only. It does not also cock or fire; the player presses again
        once the cylinder is shut.
     3. Interruptible only during the insert loop (InsertFirst / Turn / InsertNext), matching
        the interrupt edges that already exist. No new root edges.
     4. C# drives every step, like Idle / Fire / PushHammerDown.

     Changes

     1. player_rig_glb.tscn — hand control of the reload machine to C#

     Decision 4 requires the same fix applied to Hip/Aim earlier this session: an Auto edge advances
     the tree off the state C# is waiting on, so IsCurrentAnimationFinished() never returns true and
     the chart deadlocks. Flip advance_mode from Auto (2) to Enabled (1) on:

     - Rt_first_close, Rt_first_turn (out of InsertFirst)
     - Rt_next_close (out of InsertNext)
     - Rt_toclose_close, Rt_int_close, Rt_close_end
     - Rr_openhip_reload, Rr_openaim_reload, Rr_reload_hip (root level)

     Keep switch_mode = 2 (AtEnd) on all of them — that is what makes each clip finish before the next
     begins. Leave Rt_start_first as Auto: the nested machine has never been active when the reload
     first runs, and a Start() request to an inactive sub-machine is discarded (established earlier this
     session), so Start → InsertFirst must self-advance.

     Drop advance_condition = "reload_done" from Rt_first_close / Rt_next_close — C# decides now.
     The parameters/Reload/conditions/reload_done line can stay; it becomes inert.

     Add xfade_time = 0.05 to the three interrupt edges (Rt_first_int, Rt_turn_int, Rt_next_int),
     which are currently hard cuts at 0.0.

     Wire the five reload leaf nodes with node_paths for RevolverController and RigController,
     copying the form used by Idle (player_rig_glb.tscn:391-395). Add a Reloading export on
     WeaponControllers/RevolverController pointing at ../../StateMachine/Root/RevolverRig/Action/Reload.

     2. RevolverController.cs

     - public bool CanReload => ammoInCylinder < 6 && reserveAmmo > 0;
     - [Export] public State Reloading { get; set; } — the Reload compound.
     - GetInput: accept one input outside Idle — fire during a reload sets reloadInterrupted.

     public void GetInput(bool pressFire, bool aim, bool pressReload)
     {
         // The one input accepted outside Idle: fire aborts a reload in progress.
         if (Reloading is { Enabled: true })
         {
             if (pressFire) reloadInterrupted = true;
             return;
         }
         if (!CanAct) return;
         ...
         if (pressReload && CanReload) reloadTrigger = true;
         ...
     }

       Gating on CanReload at input time means a press with a full cylinder is dropped rather than
       latching in reloadTrigger to fire later. Apply the same check to the dry-gun auto-reload in
       PushHammerDown().

     - Fix the off-by-one in ReloadAddBullet(). ReloadBullet() indexes Bullets[ammoInCylinder],
       so it must run before the increment:

     public void ReloadAddBullet()
     {
         RevolverCylinderController.ReloadBullet();   // uses the pre-increment index
         AddBulletToCylinder();
         SubtractBulletFromTotalAmmo();
     }

       The same inversion exists in BulletFired() (SubtractBulletFromCylinder() runs before
       FireBullet(), which then indexes ammoInCylinder - 1). Flagged earlier and still unfixed —
       worth correcting in the same pass since both drive the same meshes.

     3. PlayerRigStates/ — the five states

     All follow the established pattern: [Export] RevolverController + [Export] RigController,
     _Ready → AddTransitions(), StateEntered → RigController.Travel(...), guards using
     IsCurrentAnimationFinished().

     Two states play two clips in sequence. Give them a _phase int, reset in StateEntered, advanced
     in StatePhysicsProcessing once the first clip finishes:

     ┌───────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │       state       │                         clip 1                         │       clip 2       │                   leaves to                   │
     ├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ IntroInsertBullet │ RevolverRigReloadStartOpenCylinder{Stance} (root leaf) │ Reload/InsertFirst │ TurnCylinder, or CloseCylinder if !CanReload  │
     ├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ TurnCylinder      │ Reload/Turn                                            │ —                  │ InsertNextBullet                              │
     ├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ InsertNextBullet  │ Reload/InsertNext                                      │ —                  │ TurnCylinder if CanReload, else CloseCylinder │
     ├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ CloseCylinder     │ Reload/ToClose                                         │ Reload/Close       │ Idle                                          │
     ├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ Interrupt         │ Reload/RevolverReloadInterrupt                         │ Reload/Close       │ Idle                                          │
     └───────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────┘

     Note the nested interrupt state is named RevolverReloadInterrupt, not Interrupt — the only
     nested state that doesn't use a short name.

     IntroInsertBullet, TurnCylinder and InsertNextBullet each also get
     AddTransition("Interrupt", () => RevolverController.reloadInterrupted). CloseCylinder does not —
     that is decision 3.

     IntroInsertBulletState.StateEntered clears reloadInterrupted so a press that arrived during a
     previous close can't leak into the next reload. InterruptState.StateEntered clears it on consume.

     Loop safety. Termination depends on ammoInCylinder rising, which depends on an animation
     method key (below). If that key is missing the loop never ends, so cap the insert count at 6 per
     reload and force CloseCylinder past that, with a GD.PushWarning naming the missing key.

     4. IdleState.cs — the entry edge

     AddTransition("Reload",
         () => RigController.IsTravelComplete() && RevolverController.reloadTrigger,
         () => RevolverController.reloadTrigger = false);

     5. Delete the temporary R-key hook

     RevolverCylinderController._Process (the [TEMP] ejecting 6 shells block) swallows the reload
     action every frame, bypasses CanAct and zeroes ammoInCylinder. It will fight the real reload.

